    "stem": "Directions: Write an essay of 160–200 words based on the following picture. In your essay, you should 1) describe the picture briefly, 2) explain its intended meaning, and 3) give your comments.",
    "referenceAnswer": "As is shown in the picture, two students are standing in front of a poster for a campus lecture. One of them says that the lecture is not related to their major and therefore is of little use, while the other believes that attending it may still be helpful.\n\nThe picture reflects a common attitude among college students: they tend to judge the value of knowledge solely by its immediate connection with their major. In my view, such a narrow view is unwise. University education is not merely professional training; it is also an opportunity to broaden one’s horizons. A lecture outside one’s field may introduce a new way of thinking, spark an unexpected interest, or help one connect ideas across disciplines. In a world where innovation often occurs at the boundaries between fields, general knowledge and curiosity are valuable assets rather than distractions.\n\nTherefore, students should be encouraged to step out of their comfort zones and attend lectures in different fields. Universities, in turn, should create a more open academic atmosphere. Only by remaining curious and open-minded can young people make the most of their education and become well-rounded individuals.",
